post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
==> Voxtty installed to /opt/voxtty

Before it will work:
  1. Add yourself to the 'input' group, then log out and back in:
       sudo usermod -aG input "$USER"
  2. Enable and start the ydotool daemon:
       sudo systemctl enable --now ydotoold
  3. Enable the user service:
       systemctl --user enable --now voxtty

Optional AI cleanup pass (off by default): put your Anthropic API key in
~/.config/voxtty/env as ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=..., then set cleanup_enabled: true
in /opt/voxtty/config.json (created on first run) and restart the service.

Press Alt+D anywhere to start/stop dictating.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'EOF'
==> Voxtty updated. Restart the service to pick up the new version:
      systemctl --user restart voxtty
EOF
}
